## FOR RECORDS (NO text of yours in any project file: copy into STATUS FOR RECORDS as RELAYED)
- The OXPd 1.x client makes HP's two string echoes of the Test service (`SyncEchoString`, `AsyncEchoString`) through `Oxpd1Echo`, with HTTP Basic for the user `guest`, never `admin`; a sync answer is read only as one text-only result alone in the response (the shapes the last gate of the Test service lane measured on `IsServiceEnabled` are refused here).
- The lab's `oxpd1 echo` makes ONE echo per run, `--pin` required; a `--password-name` holding ADMIN is a usage error and a credentials file in which any name holds ADMIN is refused before any folder or connection (exit 12; names only are read). An async echo listens on plain HTTP/1.1 (127.0.0.1 unless `--callback-bind` gives another IPv4 address), sends the device the run's own random path, and passes only on a POST there holding the message (exit 13 when none arrives within the wait). It writes nothing to a device and owes no undo.
- Named limits: the listener speaks no TLS; what a device sends and expects on its callback is UNMEASURED; the admin-name refusal reads names, not values; gate B2058's FOUND 1 (five `IsServiceEnabled` shapes) and FOUND 2 (a relative link through another link) are named as known in the READMEs and not changed.
- Nothing here has run against a device: the LAN run (the M577 to this Mac, owed 118) is a separate kit.

